  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "To find the time it takes for the number of bees to reach $40\\,000,$ we need to solve the equation $N(t)=40\\,000$ for $t,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}N(t) & =40\\,000 \\\\ 5\\,000\\cdot {2}^{t} & =40\\,000 \\\\ {2}^{t} & =\\frac{40\\,000}{5\\,000} \\\\ {2}^{t} & =\\frac{40}{5} \\\\ {2}^{t} & =8 \\\\ {2}^{t} & ={2}^{3} \\\\ t & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the number of bees increases to $40\\,000$ after $3$ months.",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
